    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1934",
    ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=cos⁡xlog⁡x,$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=cos⁡x$ and $v(x)=log⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(cos⁡x)}^{′}log⁡x+cos⁡x{(log⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =(-sin⁡x)(log⁡x)+(cos⁡x)(\\frac{1}{xln⁡10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{cos⁡x}{xln⁡10}-sin⁡xlog⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
