    ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}{e}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\sqrt{x})^{′}\\cdot {e}^{x}+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}{e}^{x}+\\sqrt{x}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
